I am excited to share that our paper <strong>"Found-RL: Foundation model-enhanced reinforcement learning via asynchronous VLM feedback for autonomous driving"</strong> has been accepted by <a href="https://www.sciopen.com/article/10.26599/COMMTR.2026.9640027">Communications in Transportation Research (COMMTR)</a>.

Found-RL is a platform that integrates foundation models (especially vision-language models) with reinforcement learning for autonomous driving, using an asynchronous batch inference framework to enable real-time learning from VLM feedback.

The paper is now available online on <a href="https://www.sciopen.com/article/10.26599/COMMTR.2026.9640027">SciOpen</a>. Code, data, and models are publicly available at <a href="https://github.com/ys-qu/found-rl">GitHub</a>.
